# Policy of this repository: DRAFT, not signed, not in force.
#
# Source: the table "Paths per Risk Level" of ADR-004 (STEMMA-160), the levels of the run-time
# operations, and the default bounds of crates/stemma-core/src/policy.rs. The owner reviews this
# file, changes it where needed, and signs it with the owner key (level 3, STEMMA-247). Whether
# this repository switches to enforcing mode is a separate decision of the owner.
stemma-policy 1

# Level 3: RBAC, keys, CI and release, policy files. The policy file and the files of the actor
# register have level 3 by the floor of the core and need no line here.
level 3 actor.rs
level 3 allowed.rs
level 3 .github/workflows/
level 3 justfile
level 3 deny.toml

# Level 2: object and store, refs, operation log, repository, index, diff computation in the
# merge path, verify, and the exclusion file (it can let a secret into history). Every path that
# no line names has level 2 as well; the lines document the table of ADR-004.
level 2 object.rs
level 2 store.rs
level 2 refs.rs
level 2 oplog.rs
level 2 repository.rs
level 2 repository/
level 2 index.rs
level 2 diff.rs
level 2 verify.rs
level 2 .stemmaignore

# Level 1: CLI, TUI, the code of the exclusion rules, and the display of diffs.
level 1 crates/stemma-cli/
level 1 crates/stemma-tui/
level 1 ignore.rs

# Level 0: docs, tests, examples. A line cannot lower what another line raises, so the tests of
# the CLI crate stay at level 1 through the line above.
level 0 docs/
level 0 adr/
level 0 README.md
level 0 tests/
level 0 fuzz/
level 0 examples/

# Run-time operations that touch no path. Only a human may purge (ADR-014).
operation purge 3
operation take-over 3
operation checkout 2
operation commit 2
operation restore 2
operation snapshot 2
operation tag 2
operation untag 2

# Agent approvals per level: the floors of the core, written down.
approvals 0 1
approvals 1 2
approvals 2 2
approvals 3 0

# Default bounds.
lease 60
weakened-level 2
